><span class="enc-snip">Henry Grattan was an Irish politician and orator who led the Patriot opposition in the Irish Parliament.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-hudson"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-hudson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry Hudson</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry Hudson was an English navigator who searched for a northern sea route to Asia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-i-count-of-champagne"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-i-count-of-champagne.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry I, Count of Champagne</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry I, called the Liberal, was count of Champagne from 1152 to 1181, son of Theobald II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-i-count-of-schwerin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-i-count-of-schwerin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry I, Count of Schwerin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry I, called the Black, was Count of Schwerin in northern Germany.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-i-duke-of-brabant"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-i-duke-of-brabant.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry I, Duke of Brabant</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry I, Duke of Brabant, was the first ruler of the Louvain dynasty to use the title Duke of Brabant, reigning from 1183 to 1235.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-i-duke-of-burgundy"><span class="enc-name">Henry I, Duke of Burgundy</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry I, known as Henry the Great, was duke of Burgundy from 965 to 1002, a son of Hugh the Great and brother of Hugh Capet.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-i-duke-of-munsterberg"><span class="enc-name">Henry I, Duke of Münsterberg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry I, Duke of Münsterberg, known as the Elder, was a son of the Bohemian king George of Poděbrady.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-castile"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-ii-of-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry II of Castile</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry II was king of Castile from 1369 to 1379, an illegitimate son of Alfonso XI.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-ii-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry II of England</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry II of England, the first Plantagenet king, ruled England, Normandy, Anjou and, through his wife Eleanor, Aquitaine, a block of lands known as the Angevin Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-france"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-ii-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry II of France</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry II of France, son of Francis I, was king of France from 1547 to 1559.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-the-pious"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-ii-the-pious.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry II the Pious</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry II the Pious was Duke of Silesia and high duke of Poland from 1238, son of Henry the Bearded and Saint Hedwig.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-count-of-rodez"><span class="enc-name">Henry II, Count of Rodez</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry II was Count of Rodez in the late 13th century, ruling the comital part of the city and lands in the Rouergue.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-duke-of-austria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-ii-duke-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry II, Duke of Austria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry II Jasomirgott, of the Babenberg family, was Margrave of Austria from 1141 and also Duke of Bavaria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-duke-of-bavaria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-ii-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry II, Duke of Bavaria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry the Quarrelsome was Duke of Bavaria from 955 to 976 and again from 985 to 995, a member of the Ottonian dynasty and cousin of Emperor Otto II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-duke-of-guise"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-ii-duke-of-guise.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry II, Duke of Guise</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry II, Duke of Guise, was a French noble of the house of Lorraine who claimed the Angevin inheritance to the throne of Naples.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-holy-roman-emperor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry II, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry II, Holy Roman Emperor, was the last Ottonian ruler, king of Germany from 1002 and emperor from 1014.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-lord-of-mecklenburg"><span class="enc-name">Henry II, Lord of Mecklenburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry II, called the Lion, was lord of Mecklenburg in the early 14th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iii-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry III of England</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry III was king of England from 1216, succeeding his father John as a nine-year-old.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-glogow"><span class="enc-name">Henry III of Głogów</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry III was a Silesian Piast duke of Głogów from 1274 and one of the most powerful princes of fragmented Poland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-the-white"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iii-the-white.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry III the White</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry III the White was a Silesian Piast duke, son of Henry II the Pious, who received Wrocław when his father's duchy was divided in 1248.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-count-of-sayn"><span class="enc-name">Henry III, Count of Sayn</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry III was Count of Sayn and the most powerful ruler of his line, governing until his death in 1247.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-holy-roman-emperor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry III, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry III, of the Salian dynasty, was king of Germany from 1039 and Holy Roman Emperor from 1046.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-landgrave-of-hesse"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iii-landgrave-of-hesse.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry III, Landgrave of Hesse</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry III (1440–1483), called the Rich, was Landgrave of Upper Hesse, ruling from Marburg after the division of Hesse in 1458.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-margrave-of-meissen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iii-margrave-of-meissen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry III, Margrave of Meissen</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry III, Margrave of Meissen, called the Illustrious, was a Wettin prince who ruled Meissen from 1221.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-castile"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iv-of-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry IV of Castile</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry IV was king of Castile from 1454 to 1474.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-england"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iv-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry IV of England</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry IV of England, Henry Bolingbroke, deposed his cousin Richard II in 1399 and founded the Lancastrian dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iv-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry IV of France</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry IV of France was king of Navarre from 1572 and the first Bourbon king of France from 1589.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-plauen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iv-of-plauen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry IV of Plauen</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry IV of Plauen was a member of the Reuss family of Vogtland lords who became Burgrave of Meissen and chancellor of the Kingdom of Bohemia under Ferdinand I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-probus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iv-probus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry IV Probus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry IV Probus was Duke of Wrocław from 1270 and High Duke of Poland at Kraków from 1288 to 1290.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-holy-roman-emperor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iv-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry IV, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry IV, Holy Roman Emperor, was king of Germany from 1056 and emperor from 1084.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-jennings"><span class="enc-name">Henry Jennings</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry Jennings was an English privateer and pirate based in Jamaica and the Bahamas.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-julius-duke-of-brunswick-luneburg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-julius-duke-of-brunswick-luneburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry Julius, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry Julius, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg, ruled the Principality of Wolfenbüttel from 1589 and was administrator of the Prince-Bishopric of Halberstadt from 1566.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-kamen"><span class="enc-name">Henry Kamen</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry Kamen is a British historian of Spain, born in Burma in 1936.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-meiggs"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-meiggs.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry Meiggs</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry Meiggs was an American railway builder who, after fleeing debts in San Francisco in 1854, built railways in Chile and then Peru.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-morgan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-morgan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry Morgan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry Morgan was a Welsh privateer based at Port Royal, Jamaica, who led raids on Spanish America, including Portobelo in 1668 and Maracaibo in 1669.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-morton-stanley"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-morton-stanley.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry Morton Stanley</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry Morton Stanley was a Welsh-American journalist and explorer who found David Livingstone in 1871 and crossed Africa in 1874–1877, following the Lualaba and Congo…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-flanders"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-of-flanders.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry of Flanders</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry of Flanders was Latin Emperor of Constantinople from 1205, succeeding his brother Baldwin I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-laach"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-of-laach.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry of Laach</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry of Laach was a German nobleman who is the first person recorded with the title count palatine of the Rhine, around 1085 to 1087.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-livonia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-of-livonia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry of Livonia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry of Livonia was a priest who took part in the German crusades in the eastern Baltic and wrote the Livonian Chronicle, covering events to 1227.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-the-palatinate"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-of-the-palatinate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry of the Palatinate</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry of the Palatinate, a Wittelsbach prince, was bishop of Utrecht from 1524 to 1529 and later of Worms and Freising.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-parkes"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-parkes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry Parkes</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry Parkes was an English-born journalist and politician who served five times as premier of New South Wales between 1872 and 1891.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-raspe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-raspe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Henry Raspe</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry Raspe was Landgrave of Thuringia from 1227 to 1247, the last of the Ludowingian dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-salt"><span class="enc-name">Henry Salt</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Henry Salt was an English artist, diplomat and collector.</span></a></li></ul>
